course: dictionary
lesson: 11962
title: Casualty: one word, several meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A casualty is a person who is hurt or killed in an accident, a war or a disaster. «The bus crash left three casualties.» Casualties means more than one casualty. The word crash is a clue: a crash is an accident, so the casualties were people who were hurt.
explain: The word can also mean something that is harmed or lost because of an event. «The old tree was a casualty of the storm» means the storm damaged or destroyed the tree. Here the casualty is a thing, not a person. Always check the words around it to see which meaning fits.
explain: In the UK, Casualty with a capital C is a hospital department for emergencies. «We took Grandma to Casualty after her fall» means the hospital emergency department, also called A&E. In the USA people say ER for the same place. When you see Casualty as a place, the sentence will usually be about being ill or hurt.
fact: A casualty is a person who is hurt or killed in an accident, war or disaster.
fact: «Casualties» is the plural of casualty: more than one casualty.
fact: In the UK, Casualty is the hospital department for emergencies, also called A&E (accident and emergency).
fact: In the USA, the same kind of place is called the ER (emergency room).
fact: «Heavy casualties» means a large number of people were hurt or killed.
exercise: «The bus crash left three casualties.» In this sentence, what does casualties mean? | Tickets for the next bus | Drivers who arrived late | *People who were hurt or killed | Buses that were fixed for free
exercise: «We took Grandma to Casualty after her fall.» In the UK, where did they go? | A shop to buy new shoes | The school library | The park for a picnic | *The hospital emergency department
exercise: In first aid class, Ruby learns to check the casualty is breathing. Who is the casualty? | *The injured person | The ambulance driver | The first aid kit | The teacher giving the lesson
test: «The old fence was a casualty of the storm.» What is the casualty in this sentence? | A row of trees | *A fence that was harmed or destroyed | The storm that blew for three days | A farmer who fixed the fence
test: The news said there were heavy casualties after the earthquake. What does heavy casualties mean? | *A large number of people hurt or killed | Many shops that opened late | Very heavy bags of rubble | A small group of visitors
exam: Which sentence uses casualty to mean the hospital emergency department in the UK? | The casualty of the storm was an old oak tree | The casualty helped the nurse carry the bags | *We waited for an hour in Casualty with my sprained wrist | Three casualties were counted after the battle
